    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a dominant score of 83.29. Facing Brown, the matchup offers a significant 13% boost in SP skill efficiency, and anchoring the order at #1 maximizes his run-scoring potential. We are also capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Lopez, J, which elevates the profiles of **Nasim Nunez** (70.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.92). Both benefit from a 19% SP skill surge and a 10% park factor; **Nasim Nunez** in particular remains a high-value start given his dual-threat ability in a league where speed scarcity makes his projected output critical to our 5x5 standing. **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** also provide high-upside plays at 63.14 and 62.64, respectively, leveraging the weak matchup against Yesavage.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Curtis Mead**, who finished with a 60.34 score\u2014strong enough to start on most days but ultimately relegated to the bench. While the favorable matchup against Lopez, J provided a substantial boost, the optimizer preferred the slightly higher reliability of our core infielders. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains on the bench (56.82) as his matchup against Burke, S is mitigated by a lower base projection relative to the high-efficiency slots occupied by **Josh Jung** and **Jacob Wilson**. We are closely monitoring the 38% rain risk surrounding **Jackson Merrill**; while his 54.34 score is decent, the weather creates a volatile floor that could lead to a truncated outing. With **Drake Baldwin** and **Andy Pages** facing tough arms in Eovaldi and Schlittler, we will need our top-order producers like **Gunnar Henderson** to drive the bulk of our offensive production today.",
